From 5cd17faaf668718c508848f5386fa6d4c0a9a66a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FIocker <4461558+FIocker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:26:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] rdna2spirv: write the compute thread-group SGPR
 (TG_SIZE_EN)

RSRC2 bit 10 adds an SGPR after the workgroup ids. The translator refused every compute
shader that sets it. None of the 2,689 carved CS does, but 91 compute programs of the
pipeline library in shaders.rpf do (docs/shader_library.md), and they read it as
s_and_b32 sN, sTG, 0xfc0, mostly followed by v_mbcnt_lo_u32_b32.

The prologue now writes it: waves in the group in [5:0], this wave's index in [11:6], 0
above. That is the GFX6-10 layout Mesa reads (ac_nir_lower_intrinsics_to_args.c:
load_num_subgroups = tg_size[5:0], load_subgroup_id = tg_size[11:6], wave64 local
invocation index = mbcnt(~0, tg_size & 0xfc0)). Thread i is in wave i / W, as for
s_get_waveid_in_workgroup. Not measured on hardware.

tests/semantic/test_cs_tg_size.py runs it on the CPU (local index through the 0xfc0 field
in wave32 and wave64, 1-D and 3-D groups, the wave count with a partial wave, the whole
value, the register after three workgroup ids). The two tests that pinned the refusal now
check that it translates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
